{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":69322,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"827b799b0e768bbedc68e39c783ea5f7d812b1db4609629bd4384056aeaae3bf","packTokens":29795,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":236,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"drafts","tokens":29322,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"merge"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMerge three independent spec drafts into one spec (same format rules as the drafts).\nEvery merged requirement lists in \"alignment\" which draft requirements it came from, as \"d<draft>:<REQ-id>\" (e.g. \"d1:REQ-2\"). Keep a requirement even if only one draft has it. Never write a requirement that is in no draft.\nWhen drafts conflict, keep both readings as separate requirements and add a conflict entry. Renumber merged requirements REQ-1.. and their ACs AC-<req>.<n>.\nEach Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes. Reword a draft's Then that doesn't, without changing what it checks.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"drafts\" kind=\"spec-drafts\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d1\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"The driver application requirement is delivered as a responsive, installable web app usable in a phone browser; no native application or app-store release is part of this web product.\",\n   \"The stated staff and customer identity flows use Meridian Microsoft sign-in for staff and customer email/password plus an emailed one-time code and emailed reset link, as assumed in ASM-23.\",\n   \"The web app presents access, persistence, account revocation, and workflow outcomes returned by the separate API; API authorization and data isolation are not asserted by UI requirements.\",\n   \"ASM-2 and ASM-18 conflict on whether a temperature-history gap alone places stock On Hold. The web app therefore shows the API-returned gap review and stock status without choosing that server policy.\",\n   \"Warehouse-local time governs cutoff, working-day, delivery-date, and route rules, with dates and times displayed in the user's local zone and the warehouse zone identified, per ASM-6 and ASM-27.\",\n   \"The numeric policy values are fixed as assumed in ASM-4, including the 15-minute silence interval, two-minute alert target, 25% budget warning, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction.\",\n   \"The logger gateway and inbound export use the supplier's documented interface and file format described by ASM-8 and ASM-21; gateway ingestion is API-side.\",\n   \"The web UI supports the assumed latest-two browser versions and WCAG 2.1 AA main flows in ASM-13, ASM-14, ASM-25, and ASM-26.\",\n   \"The source request ends during US-009; driver web behavior is limited to intent spans and explicit Q-3 and Q-4 decisions, and no unstated remainder of that user story is inferred.\",\n   \"Recall response quantities and dispositions follow ASM-15 and ASM-19; supporting documents are not required by the assumed response policy.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"320–1920 CSS-pixel viewport widths; minimum 44 × 44 CSS-pixel touch targets at narrow widths\",\n    \"text\": \"Every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, and touch controls on narrow layouts have targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"WCAG 2.1 AA conformance on 100% of the agreed main flows\",\n    \"text\": \"The main staff, customer, and driver web flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"4 browser families × 2 latest versions\",\n    \"text\": \"The portals support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"API-SIDE: durable shared-record persistence, server-side role and organisation enforcement, session revocation, server-side validation and status transitions, allocation concurrency and policy calculations, stock expiry processing, and database-level audit retention; the web requirements cover presentation of API responses.\",\n   \"API-SIDE: supplier-gateway batch ingestion, reading deduplication and reordering, sensor-scale ingestion at 5,000 concurrent devices, silence and excursion detection, stability-budget recalculation, hold placement, and the two-minute alert deadline; the web requirements cover the returned histories, statuses, and alerts.\",\n   \"API-SIDE: delivery of email alerts and password-reset or one-time-code messages. SMS and native push channels are excluded by ASM-10 and ASM-22; the driver experience is a responsive web app, not a native iOS or Android app.\",\n   \"Historical spreadsheet or paper-record import is excluded by ASM-7 and ASM-20; initial setup uses seed data.\",\n   \"A full immutable audit trail beyond the assumed creator and last-change identity and timestamps is excluded by ASM-11 and ASM-24.\",\n   \"A custom report builder is excluded by ASM-12.\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The sign-in page is open and the user selects staff sign-in\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option and does not show a customer password form\",\n      \"when\": \"The user continues to the staff sign-in flow\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The customer sign-in page is open and the API accepts the email and password but requires a second step\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows a one-time-code entry field and a submit control\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer submits the credentials\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer requests a password reset\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the reset-request confirmation returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"The reset request is submitted\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide Meridian staff sign-in through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer sign-in through email and password followed by a one-time code, with an emailed password-reset link.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"ASM-23\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.96\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns records scoped to a customer's organisation or a staff member's assigned warehouses\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows only the returned records and no edit controls are shown for an Auditor\",\n      \"when\": \"The user opens the corresponding list screen\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An active session becomes invalid and the API returns an unauthorized response\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the sign-in page and an access-expired message\",\n      \"when\": \"The user opens a protected page\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an authenticated user opens a portal view, the Meridian responsive web app shall show only the records and actions returned for that user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation, and shall present Auditor views as read-only.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-17\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.95\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens user management for their organisation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the invitation status returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"The administrator enters an invitee and submits the invitation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses a user removal or invitation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned error message and does not show a success confirmation\",\n      \"when\": \"The administrator submits the action\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users through controls scoped to the administrator's own customer organisation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-7\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.9\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The product list contains products with names and codes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the matching product list returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"A System Administrator searches by a product name or code\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator submits a product deactivation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the product as deactivated\",\n      \"when\": \"The API returns the updated product status\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let System Administrators list products, search by name or code, view product details, and deactivate a product.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-10\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.9\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator opens the temperature-profile editor\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the entered profile fields and any validation error returned for an overlapping or incomplete tier\",\n      \"when\": \"The administrator enters a band, tiers, reason, and effective date\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product has more than one profile version\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows that version's values and no edit controls\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens an earlier version\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where a System Administrator edits a product temperature profile, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture its storage band, non-overlapping contiguous tiers and their allowance or not-permitted designation, plus a change reason and effective date, and show earlier versions as read-only.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.89\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a new effective profile version and recalculated values for held stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the new version's effective date and the returned budget and decision values\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the profile and affected stock views\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When an effective-dated temperature-profile version changes, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the new version and the recalculated budgets and decisions returned for stock still held from its effective date onward.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"Q-8\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.84\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens the receipt form\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the submitted receipt details, the returned Quarantined status, and the returned inbound budget\",\n      \"when\": \"The operator enters receipt details and uploads an accepted inbound logger file\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses a receipt with an expired lot date or an unsupported logger file\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned error message next to the relevant field\",\n      \"when\": \"The operator submits the receipt\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a Warehouse Operator records a receipt, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location, accept the inbound logger file, and show the returned quarantine status and inbound budget before a release decision.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"ASM-9\",\n     \"ASM-21\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.9\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns on-hand quantities and status quantities for a product, lot, and warehouse\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the on-hand total and each returned status quantity as a separate breakdown row\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the stock view\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns stock rows for more than one lot or warehouse\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows only the rows matching the selected filter values\",\n      \"when\": \"A user filters the stock list\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall present on-hand stock with mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, and show the returned warehouse, lot, product, and receipt details.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-3\",\n     \"ASM-12\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.9\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns two handling units from one lot with different temperature histories\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows separate rows with each unit's quantity, history, and returned budget values\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the lot's handling-unit view\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When portions of received stock have different temperature histories, the Meridian responsive web app shall show them as separate handling units with their returned quantity, temperature history, and tier budget used and remaining.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"Q-5\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.86\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Officer opens a decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted range\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the proposal and its returned status without showing an approval confirmation\",\n      \"when\": \"The officer proposes a disposition\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses approval by the proposing person or a user without the Quality Manager role\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned error message and the decision remains shown as unapproved\",\n      \"when\": \"That user attempts the approval\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"Where stock has been exposed to a not-permitted temperature range, the Meridian responsive web app shall present a Quality Officer proposal step and a separate Quality Manager approval step for a different person.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"Q-1\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.9\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user opens the order form\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the complete order summary before submission\",\n      \"when\": \"The user selects products, quantities, a saved address, an eligible date, and a fulfilment choice\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns eligible dates for the serving warehouse\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows only the returned eligible dates and identifies the warehouse time zone\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer opens the delivery-date selector\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let customer users create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, an organisation-saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-27\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.89\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns an order with line quantities and a status before Packed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows each line's allocated and outstanding quantities and the change and cancel controls\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer opens the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns an order status of Packed or later\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the current status and no change or cancel controls\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer opens the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer cancellation is accepted by the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned Cancelled status and updated quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer refreshes the order view\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer views or changes an order, the Meridian responsive web app shall show its status and allocated and outstanding quantities for each line, and expose change or cancellation controls only while the order is not Packed.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"I-11\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.89\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a line allocated across multiple lots\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows each lot and its allocated quantity separately\",\n      \"when\": \"A dispatcher or customer opens the order line\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits a lot override that the API refuses for eligibility reasons\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned error message and the unchanged allocation list\",\n      \"when\": \"The response is displayed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show order allocations by line and lot, expose dispatcher lot-override controls with a required reason, and show the allocation or override outcome returned by the API.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"I-17\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.88\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens the packing screen\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned box contents, logger, and sealing details\",\n      \"when\": \"The operator selects stock, a box type, and a logger and submits the packing action\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses a box with an incompatible storage band or an already-associated logger\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned error message and no sealed status\",\n      \"when\": \"The operator submits the packing action\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show box contents and sealing details returned by the API.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-12\",\n     \"I-13\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.88\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Dispatcher creates a route\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the ordered route summary using the warehouse time zone\",\n      \"when\": \"The Dispatcher enters a vehicle, driver, date, stops, and planned arrival times\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses confirmation because a box exceeds its qualified duration less the safety margin\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the affected box and the returned exceedance amount\",\n      \"when\": \"The Dispatcher submits route confirmation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a change to a confirmed route\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the changed stop or schedule details returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"The driver opens the route view\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Dispatchers create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times, and shall display route-confirmation errors and confirmed route changes returned by the API.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-12\",\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"ASM-27\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.88\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns readings, a gap, and an out-of-order or otherwise flagged reading\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the readings in their returned event-time order, a visible gap, the applicable band, and the reading flag\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens the temperature-history view\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API marks a device silent after the configured 15-minute interval\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the silent status returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"A user opens its device or route view\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns the same history in chart and table data\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the corresponding returned history in each view\",\n      \"when\": \"A user switches between the chart and table views\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show temperature history for boxes, cold rooms, and lots as a chart and table with readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, and returned reading flags or silence status.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.87\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns an open excursion, its handling units, and their hold statuses\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the excursion, affected handling units, tier budgets, and returned hold statuses\",\n      \"when\": \"A Quality Officer opens the excursion view\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a remaining-budget warning or a not-permitted-range alert\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the alert type and affected stock or device\",\n      \"when\": \"A Dispatcher or Quality Officer opens the alerts view\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When the API returns an excursion or stability-budget alert, the Meridian responsive web app shall show its affected device or stock, excursion status, tier usage and remaining allowance, and returned hold status.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-10\",\n     \"ASM-18\",\n     \"ASM-22\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.86\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a quality-review case linked to a delivered customer order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-18.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the case status and the affected delivered line returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"The customer or authorized staff user opens the related order or case view\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When corrected temperature history identifies an excursion affecting stock already delivered, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the returned quality-review case to the relevant customer and staff users.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-14\"\n    ],\n    \"stability\": 0.84\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver has opened today's assigned route while connected and then loses connectivity\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the route and its stops while offline\",\n      \"when\": \"The driver opens the cached route\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver records an action while offline and connectivity returns\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the synchronization result returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"The web app synchronizes the queued action\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A queued action is submitted after the API reports the driver's account disabled\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-19.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"The screen shows the returned rejection message and does not show the action as synchronized\",\n      \"when\": \"Synchronization is attempted\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide an installable, responsive driver web experience that caches today's assigned route and records loading and delivery actions for synchronization when the browser reconnects.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n