e lot detail page\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian web application shall show stock location changes and a reconciled, mutually exclusive quantity breakdown for each product, lot, and warehouse.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-7\",\n     \"ASM-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator opens organisation settings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request identifies the address change and the screen shows the address list returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"the user adds, edits, or removes a saved delivery address\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator opens a customer organisation's settings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request includes the organisation-level shelf-life value and the screen shows the saved value returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator sets its minimum remaining shelf life\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user opens the order form\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires at least one line, a quantity of at least one pack per line, a saved delivery address, a requested delivery date, and a choice between deliver-what-is-available and deliver-complete-only\",\n      \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The user selects a delivery date before or after the serving warehouse cut-off, or selects a configured holiday or non-working day\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the earliest permitted delivery date based on the serving warehouse's configured cut-off, working days, and holidays\",\n      \"when\": \"the date choices are displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user submits an order and the API returns its order details\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.5\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the order status and each line's allocated and outstanding quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"the order page is displayed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer user prepares an order, the Meridian web application shall support selecting an organisation address, delivery date, products, quantities, and the order-completion preference.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"ASM-5\",\n     \"ASM-6\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An order has not reached Packed status\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers change and cancel controls and a repeated submission while the first submission is pending produces only one order-submission request\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer user opens the order page\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An order is Packed or later\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers no change or cancel control and shows the current status returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer user opens its order page\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher cancels an order after packing begins or a customer cancels an eligible order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the cancellation response and the returned stock availability count\",\n      \"when\": \"the cancellation is submitted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API refuses an order change or cancellation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned error message and retains the returned order status and line quantities\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits the action\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a customer user changes or cancels an order, the Meridian web application shall offer the action only before packing and shall show the resulting order and allocation state returned by the API.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"Q-6\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An order has been allocated\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists each allocated lot, expiry date, quantity, and line split returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens its allocation details\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Dispatcher selects an alternative lot\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request includes the chosen lot and reason and the screen shows the accepted allocation or the API's refusal message\",\n      \"when\": \"the dispatcher submits an override with a reason\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports a back order or an order that must remain complete-only until all lines can be filled\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the outstanding quantities and the returned allocation status\",\n      \"when\": \"the dispatcher opens the order\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports allocated stock as On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the removed allocation, any replacement allocation, and the returned notification outcome\",\n      \"when\": \"the dispatcher opens the affected order\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a dispatcher reviews allocations, the Meridian web application shall display the returned lot splits and stock outcomes and provide a reasoned override control subject to the API decision.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-11\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"Q-6\",\n     \"Q-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator packs stock into a shipper box\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned compatibility result and prevents submission when the API reports a storage-band or box-type mismatch\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator selects products, lots, a box type, and a logger barcode\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A box is ready to be sealed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows that exactly one logger is required and, after sealing, displays the returned seal time, operator, contents, quantities, and logger\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator opens its sealing action\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher creates a route\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for one vehicle, one driver, a route date, and at least one ordered stop with a planned arrival time\",\n      \"when\": \"the route form is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A dispatcher confirms a route whose box exceeds its qualified duration less the configured safety margin at the planned arrival\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the affected box and the returned overage amount\",\n      \"when\": \"the API refuses confirmation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before the driver has left for an affected stop\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.5\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request identifies the changed route and the screen shows the returned stop order and driver notification status\",\n      \"when\": \"the dispatcher moves or reorders the stop\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When warehouse staff pack stock and dispatchers plan routes, the Meridian web application shall present box compatibility, logger assignment, stop scheduling, and route-confirmation results returned by the API.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-12\",\n     \"I-15\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens a box, cold-room, or lot temperature history\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen provides chart and table views with readings positioned by reading time and with the product band and excursions marked\",\n      \"when\": \"the API returns history data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns duplicate or delayed readings, readings out of order, or readings marked as future-dated or before sealing\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned reading times, identifies invalid-for-calculation readings, and displays the corrected history in time order\",\n      \"when\": \"the history is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports a temperature-history gap or a device silent for 15 minutes\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the gap or silent state distinctly and does not draw readings across a gap as if they were recorded\",\n      \"when\": \"a user views the history or device status\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns logger gateway batch readings or an inbound logger file's reading results\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-12.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the returned readings and their associated device or receipt\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the relevant device or receipt history\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a user views temperature monitoring, the Meridian web application shall show the returned reading history, temperature gaps, device state, and excursion markers for boxes, cold rooms, and lots.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"ASM-2\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns an excursion that opens on an out-of-band reading and closes after three consecutive in-band readings\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned excursion start, end, readings, and closure status\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the excursion detail\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API returns a handling unit's budget use and remaining allowance\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows used and remaining amounts by tier and the excursions charged to each tier\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens its budget detail\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An effective profile version change has caused the API to recalculate affected stock budgets or decisions\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned recalculated budgets and decision status from the effective date onward\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the affected stock or profile detail\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports a new excursion or an unresolved reading gap affecting stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned On Hold or quality-review status before a disposition is displayed as final\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the affected stock detail\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports an excursion, silence, low remaining budget, used-up tier, not-permitted range, or a correction to an earlier excursion\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.5\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned alert category, recipient role, delivery channel, sent time, and corrected excursion or budget status when present\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the alert or excursion history\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The API reports a late-discovered excursion affecting stock already delivered\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-13.6\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned quality-review case and affected delivery details\",\n      \"when\": \"the affected customer or staff user opens the case\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When temperature-history or budget data changes an excursion assessment, the Meridian web application shall display the returned excursion, handling-unit budget, hold, decision, and alert status.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-13\",\n     \"I-14\",\n     \"Q-2\",\n     \"Q-5\",\n     \"Q-8\",\n     \"ASM-4\",\n     \"ASM-10\",\n     \"ASM-18\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver has signed in and opened the current workday route while online\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen continues to show the cached route, stops, and delivery details for that workday\",\n      \"when\": \"the device loses its network connection\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver records an offline load, route, or delivery action\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the action as queued and retains its entered values until synchronization is attempted\",\n      \"when\": \"the action is saved without a connection\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A queued driver action is synchronized after the user's account has been disabled or removed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the synchronization error and does not show the action as accepted into the shared record\",\n      \"when\": \"the API refuses the action\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The driver reconnects with an enabled account\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-14.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned synchronization result for each queued action\",\n      \"when\": \"queued actions synchronize\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a driver uses the route workflow, the Meridian web application shall provide an installable responsive web experience that keeps the current workday route available offline and queues supported driver actions until connectivity returns.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-4\",\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-4\",\n     \"ASM-1\",\n     \"ASM-17\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A driver opens a delivery handover form\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requires the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgement of receipt and does not require a drawn signature\",\n      \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A delivery is refused or only partly completed\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request includes delivered and undelivered quantities and the refusal or partial-delivery reason and the screen shows the returned outstanding quantity\",\n      \"when\": \"the driver records the handover\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The warehouse receives undelivered stock and any required quality check is pending or complete\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-15.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned receipt and quality-check status and shows stock as available only when the API reports it available\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens the return-stock status\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a driver records a delivery handover, the Meridian web application shall collect recipient acknowledgement and quantities delivered or left outstanding.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-15\",\n     \"I-10\",\n     \"Q-3\",\n     \"Q-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager opens a recall record\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists the returned locations and deliveries for the lot and identifies remaining stock reported as blocked\",\n      \"when\": \"the recall detail is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user opens an affected delivery recall response form\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen provides fields for response, quantity, and stated disposition for each affected delivery and quantity categories for located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted for units\",\n      \"when\": \"the form is displayed\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer submits a recall quantity reconciliation\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the submitted quantities, stated dispositions, and returned accounted-for status without requiring supporting-document upload\",\n      \"when\": \"the API returns the response status\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A recall still has unreconciled quantities\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-16.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the outstanding quantity count and the affected customer responses returned by the API\",\n      \"when\": \"a Quality Manager opens its progress page\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"When a lot is recalled, the Meridian web application shall show the returned affected-stock and delivery list, remaining-stock block status, and customer response reconciliation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"Q-1\",\n     \"ASM-15\",\n     \"ASM-19\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens a stock, order, temperature-history, or recall list\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the filtered record list and the downloaded file contains the records returned for that filter\",\n      \"when\": \"the user applies available filters or requests CSV export\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens an eligible record detail\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the creator, last changer, and their timestamps as read-only fields\",\n      \"when\": \"the API returns creator and last-changer fields\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user opens an Auditor view\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-17.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers no record mutation controls and shows the returned record history as read-only\",\n      \"when\": \"the record or history is displayed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian web application shall provide filtered on-screen record lists, CSV export, and read-only record details that display creator and last-changer identity and timestamps when returned.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-6\",\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"I-17\",\n     \"ASM-11\",\n     \"ASM-12\",\n     \"ASM-24\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A user selects English or Arabic\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-18.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen displays the selected language and, for Arabic, uses right-to-left text direction and page flow\",\n      \"when\": \"the selected locale is applied\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian web application shall let users select English or Arabic and shall render Arabic pages and text right to left.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-16\",\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\",\n     \"ASM-14\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"suggestions\": []\n },\n {\n  \"draft\": \"d3\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"ASM-1 and ASM-17: queued driver actions are not accepted if the account is disabled or removed before synchronization; the web app displays the API refusal.\",\n   \"ASM-2 and ASM-18 conflict on gap disposition. The web app displays the API-returned review and stock status and does not infer a temperature tier; confirm the intended server status policy.\",\n   \"ASM-3 and Q-7: the quantity view presents on-hand total and mutually exclusive status quantities.\",\n   \"ASM-4: the stated 15-minute silence, two-minute alert target, 25-percent remaining-budget alert, three consecutive in-band readings, and 30-day expiry restriction are fixed values; server timing and policy calculations are API-SIDE.\",\n   \"ASM-5 and Q-6: System Administrators set one minimum shelf-life value per customer organisation; customers and Dispatchers cannot set it per order.\",\n   \"ASM-6 and ASM-27: warehouse-local time governs cut-offs, working days, holidays, delivery dates, and route times; the UI identifies the warehouse time zone and displays dates and times in the user's local zone.\",\n   \"ASM-8 and ASM-21: supplier gateway and inbound logger file interfaces use Meridian's documented supplier contract; the exact accepted upload formats require the supplied interface documentation.\",\n   \"ASM-9: uploaded images and PDFs are limited to 10 MB each where those file types apply.\",\n   \"ASM-10 and ASM-22: alerts use email-only fixed templates; no SMS or push notification is specified.\",\n   \"ASM-11 and ASM-24: records expose creator and last-changer identity and times; a full audit trail is not specified.\",\n   \"ASM-12: supported operational views are filtered on-screen lists and CSV exports, with no custom report builder.\",\n   \"ASM-13 and ASM-25: supported browsers are the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n   \"ASM-14 and ASM-26: WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.\",\n   \"ASM-15 and ASM-19: customer recall responses record quantity and disposition per affected delivery and reconcile quantities as located, used, returned, disposed of, or otherwise accounted for; supporting documents are not required.\",\n   \"ASM-16 and ASM-28: system planning volumes are up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year, in addition to the stated 5,000 reporting devices; backend capacity is API-SIDE.\",\n   \"The supplied request ends at the US-009 Description heading; driver web requirements are limited to the described intent and answers.\"\n  ],\n  \"nfrs\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n    \"metric\": \"At viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1440 CSS pixels, page horizontal overflow is 0 pixels; on the 320-pixel viewport, each primary interactive target is at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.\",\n    \"text\": \"Every portal page is responsive for phone, tablet, and desktop layouts, with touch-sized interactive controls on phone viewports.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n    \"metric\": \"Pass the main portal flows on 8 browser/version combinations: two latest versions for each of 4 named browsers.\",\n    \"text\": \"The responsive portals support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n    \"metric\": \"0 unmet WCAG 2.1 AA success criteria in the audited main flows.\",\n    \"text\": \"The main portal flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"outOfScope\": [\n   \"API-SIDE: database persistence, transactional stock and allocation invariants, server-side identity verification and organisation isolation, workflow state transitions, temperature-reading ingestion and recalculation, excursion detection and alert/email delivery deadlines, expiry processing, audit retention, and recall blocking are proved by the separate API run; the web requirements cover the screens and requests using API responses.\",\n   \"Historical spreadsheet and paper-record migration is excluded under ASM-7 and ASM-20; the platform starts empty with setup seed data.\",\n   \"Native iOS/Android binaries and app-store publication are excluded by the web-only platform constraint; the requested driver functions are specified in the responsive web app.\"\n  ],\n  \"requirements\": [\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A signed-in staff user or customer user has portal access\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-1.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows links to the modules permitted for that user, including the applicable stock, order, delivery, temperature, quality, and recall pages\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens the portal navigation\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide role-oriented portal pages for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-1\",\n     \"I-2\",\n     \"I-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff user opens the sign-in page\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen offers sign-in through the Meridian Microsoft account flow and does not offer an external staff-account option\",\n      \"when\": \"the user selects staff sign-in\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user enters an email address and password\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen requests the one-time code step before showing the customer portal\",\n      \"when\": \"the customer submits the sign-in form\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user requests a password reset\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-2.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows a confirmation that a reset link was requested by email\",\n      \"when\": \"the user submits the reset form\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall present separate sign-in flows for staff using a Meridian Microsoft account and customer users using email, password, and a one-time code.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-7\",\n     \"ASM-23\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A staff user is assigned to a subset of warehouses\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists records only for the assigned warehouses returned for that session\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens a stock, order, or route list\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Manager or Auditor opens a warehouse-scoped list\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows records for all warehouses returned for that role\",\n      \"when\": \"the list loads\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer user belongs to one organisation and the API refuses access to another organisation's record\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-denied message and no other-organisation record fields\",\n      \"when\": \"the user opens that record's route or follows its link\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"An Auditor opens a record page\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-3.4\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows record details without create, edit, or delete controls\",\n      \"when\": \"the page renders\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show records and actions according to the signed-in user's role, warehouse assignments, and customer organisation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator is signed in\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows user-management actions scoped to that administrator's organisation\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator opens user management\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Customer Administrator submits an invite or removal request\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the refusal message and does not show the other organisation's user as changed\",\n      \"when\": \"the API refuses a user from another organisation\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A signed-in user has been disabled or removed and the API refuses the next online request\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-4.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows an access-ended message and the protected page's record fields are cleared\",\n      \"when\": \"the web app receives that refusal\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users only within that administrator's customer organisation.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-7\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator creates or edits a product profile\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows a validation error identifying the missing or invalid profile fields\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator submits a profile with no temperature band or with overlapping or gapped tiers\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A System Administrator enters a valid profile\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-5.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the request contains the storage-band bounds and each tier's bounds and allowance in hours and minutes or its not-permitted value\",\n      \"when\": \"the administrator saves the profile\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide product-profile forms for a storage band and stability-budget tiers, including tiers marked not permitted.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A product has multiple profile versions returned by the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-6.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists each version with its reason, effective date, and creator, and earlier-version fields have no edit controls\",\n      \"when\": \"a user opens profile history\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show product-profile versions with their reason, effective date, and creator, and shall show earlier versions as read-only.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"Products are available in the portal\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen lists the matching returned products and shows each product's active or deactivated status\",\n      \"when\": \"a user searches by product name or code\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A customer selects a deactivated product for an order\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-7.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows that the product cannot be ordered and provides no orderable quantity field for it\",\n      \"when\": \"the order form loads its product status\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide product lists searchable by name or code and show deactivated products as unavailable for ordering.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-10\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator opens stock receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows fields for product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf\",\n      \"when\": \"the receipt form renders\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator submits a receipt with a past expiry date or a required field missing\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the error message beside the relevant receipt field\",\n      \"when\": \"the API returns a refusal or field error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt is accepted by the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-8.3\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the receipt record and its Quarantined status\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator opens its receipt details\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide a stock-receipt form for the product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator is viewing a receipt\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the uploaded file and the returned inbound readings and budget use before the release controls\",\n      \"when\": \"the operator uploads a logger file accepted by the configured supplier interface\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator uploads a file rejected by the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-9.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned file error message and no successful-upload indicator\",\n      \"when\": \"the upload response is displayed\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide an inbound logger-file upload and show the returned inbound temperature history and budget use before a release decision.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-5\",\n     \"I-8\",\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"ASM-8\",\n     \"ASM-9\",\n     \"ASM-21\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt is Quarantined and a Quality Officer opens it\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the returned receipt data, temperature-budget use, and release decision controls\",\n      \"when\": \"the receipt review page renders\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A receipt is within 30 days of expiry on arrival or otherwise refused release by the API\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-10.2\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the API's refusal message and the receipt remains displayed with its returned status\",\n      \"when\": \"the Quality Officer submits a release decision\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show Quality Officers the receipt review and release controls and the API's refusal for stock that cannot be released.\",\n    \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n    \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n    \"sources\": [\n     \"I-9\",\n     \"ASM-4\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"acceptance\": [\n     {\n      \"given\": \"A Quality Officer proposes a disposition for affected stock\",\n      \"id\": \"AC-REQ-11.1\",\n      \"level\": \"ui\",\n      \"then\": \"the screen shows the proposal as awaiting approval and does not show an approval action to that same user\",\n      \"when\": \"the proposal is submitted\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"given\": \"The proposing Quality Officer opens the pending disposition\",\n   